# Documentation placement

- Cursor rules = persistent constraints
- Cursor skills = procedures for a specific activity
- `docs/sdlc/` = lifecycle orchestration
- `docs/product/` = business/product truth (do not invent)
- `docs/requirements/`, `user-stories/`, `bdd/` = specification artifacts
- `docs/test-*` and `docs/bugs/` = QA artifacts
- `docs/architecture/` and `docs/adr/` = technical decisions
- `docs/ai/` = AI operating model
- `src/` = application implementation (does not exist in ENG-001)
- `.github/workflows/` = CI automation

Do not put process rules only in chat. Update the canonical file.
Do not treat example IDs in templates as real BankCRM features.
